# Lenses Studio and Classic parity

forge-lenses ships **two** user interfaces over the **same** Python server and JSON APIs:

- **Lenses Studio** — React SPA at `/studio/` (`lenses-enterprise/` → `lenses/static/studio/`).
- **Classic Lenses** — Server-rendered HTML from `lenses/render.py`.

**Studio first:** Prefer implementing new user-visible behavior in **Studio** first.

**Classic in sync:** Duplicate the capability in **Classic** so both surfaces stay equivalent (same features; presentation may differ). A change that only lands in Studio should include a Classic follow-up or an explicit exception (note/ADR).

Do **not** assume Classic will be removed or merged into Studio.

See `docs/adr-001-lenses-studio-shell.md` and `lenses/website/interface-pages.md`.
